Vendored third-party sources (Grounded-SAM-2, byte_track, cython_bbox) — not ROS packages
and not built by this workspace. colcon otherwise discovers cython_bbox's setup.py and
fails the whole `colcon build`, which is why builds here used --packages-select and
silently left packages like tare_planner out of install/.

Nothing under ai_module/src imports these: sam_mapper carries its own port of the 3D
back-end (see docs/M2_perception.md 3.6-split) and the ByteTrack/spaCy front-end it needed
is superseded by SAM 3. semantic_mapper itself is a plain pyproject package run directly
(ros2_system.py), not via colcon, so ignoring this subtree changes nothing for it.
